#### **TRANSMITTER**

The proposed VLC-OCC-CDMA system employs a multiple sub-codes structure and LEDs with different peak wavelengths to separate the signals carried by different sub-codes.

The transmitter model of the VLC-OCC-CDMA system is shown in Fig. 1. Transmitters are LEDs and use on-off keying (OOK) modulation.  $b^{(k)}$  is the signal of the kth user after modulation. Each user data is copied to M data streams, and  $b^{(k)}_m$  is the mth data stream of the kth user, where  $m \in \{1, 2, \cdots, M\}$ , and  $k \in \{1, 2, \cdots, K\}$ . The VLC-OCC-CDMA system uses a set of optical complementary codes OCC(N, M, M,  $\lambda_a$ ,  $\lambda_c$ ) as the signature codes for K users. Assume that the OCC assigned to user k is  $\mathbf{C}^{(k)} = \{\mathbf{c}^{(k)}_m\}_{m=1}^M$ ,  $k \in \{1, 2, \cdots, K\}$ , where  $\mathbf{c}^{(k)}_m = [\mathbf{c}^{(k)}_{m,1}, \mathbf{c}^{(k)}
